<%- include('../partials/head') %>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Legal Resources</h1>
  <div class="rule"></div>
  <p class="lead">Useful information to add to your legal search.</p>
</div>

<div class="list">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Questions to ask an attorney</h3>
    <p class="small muted">Come prepared to your consultation with a clear list of what you need to know — experience with similar cases, likely timeline, communication style, and cost.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>How attorney fees may work</h3>
    <p class="small muted">Attorneys may bill hourly, charge a flat fee, or work on contingency depending on the type of case. Ask up front how fees are structured.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>What to bring to a consultation</h3>
    <p class="small muted">Relevant documents, a timeline of events, contact information for other parties involved, and a list of questions.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>How legal referrals work</h3>
    <p class="small muted">Referral platforms like Attorney Menu connect you with attorneys who may be able to help — the choice to hire is always yours.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Understanding contingency fees</h3>
    <p class="small muted">In a contingency arrangement, an attorney is paid a percentage of any recovery, and typically nothing if the case doesn't succeed.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Preparing a case timeline</h3>
    <p class="small muted">A written timeline of key dates and events helps your attorney understand your situation quickly and accurately.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Gathering important documents</h3>
    <p class="small muted">Contracts, correspondence, medical records, police reports, and photos are commonly useful depending on your case type.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Legal terms explained</h3>
    <p class="small muted">Plain-language explanations of common legal terms you may encounter while researching your situation.</p>
  </div>
</div>

